  "performance_interpretation": {
    "observed": "All three reduced-precision modes pass the isolated correctness guard, but each loses both S1 and S2 to FP32. The losses do not reverse under two-stream contention.",
    "resource_fact": "All four modes retain the same 320 physical TMEM-column footprint and the same M128N128/q2/kv24 one-wave schedule, so the dtype change does not create the resource-residency reduction that motivated the transfer hypothesis.",
    "typed_overhead": "QK16 adds a packed TMEM load plus immediate FP32 upcast for softmax. PV16 adds typed pack/unpack and FP32 rescale arithmetic with FP16 RNE writeback. The measured direction is consistent with these boundary costs dominating any narrower accumulator benefit.",
    "profiling_policy": "Because isolated S2 already regressed by 5.60-13.53%, the fixed gate rejected every FP16 mode before whole-graph NSYS, NCU, long throughput, or request replay. No resource claim beyond the statically invariant physical layout is made."
  },
